The {{Term/Store|Fierce Deity Armor||Series, TFH, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|TFH, BotW, TotK}}<ref name="E 123"/><ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{TFH|-}}===
{{Descriptions TFH}}
The Fierce Deity Armor is an [[Outfit]] that was added in the Ver. 2.0.0 update of {{TFH}}. It is obtained by completing the [[Den of Trials]] for the first time. When worn, the Fierce Deity Armor will double the power of [[Link]]'s [[Sword]] and also allow Link to shoot four [[Sword Beam]]s in a cross shape when the Sword is swung, provided his [[Heart Meter|Hearts]] is full. The Sword Beams can be alternatively be fired from the Sword when performing a [[Spin Attack]], even when the Hearts is not full. Additionally, Link will remain steadfast at all times and won't get knocked back from [[Enemies in Tri Force Heroes|Enemies]] while wearing the Fierce Deity Armor.

Any [[Links]] who join the game through [[Download Play]] will be unable to obtain the Fierce Deity Armor.

==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Fierce Deity Armor is a piece of [[Armor]] in {{BotW}}. It is obtained by scanning the {{MM|-}} [[Link]] [[amiibo]] with the [[Amiibo (Ability)|amiibo]] [[Rune]]. According to its description, the Fierce Deity Armor is the same armor as the one worn by [[Fierce Deity Link]] in the [[Era of the Hero of Time]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> When worn, the Fierce Deity Armor provides one level of [[Attack Up]]. The Fierce Deity Armor can be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]], but it cannot be [[Dye|Hateno Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. The Fierce Deity Armor, alongside the [[Fierce Deity Boots]] and [[Fierce Deity Mask]], compose the [[Fierce Deity Set]].

